# Machine-specific values for camera-server.service, sourced via its
# EnvironmentFile=. Copy this file to wherever that directive points (e.g.
# /etc/camera-server.env) and fill in both values for your machine -- the
# unit refuses to start if the file at that path is missing, rather than
# silently falling back to something wrong.
#
# Not folded into the unit file itself: unlike these two, User= and
# SupplementaryGroups= in camera-server.service can't be set this way --
# systemd only expands ${VAR} from Environment=/EnvironmentFile= inside Exec*
# command lines (systemd.exec(5)), never in plain directives like User=. So
# those two stay literal, CHANGE-FOR-YOUR-MACHINE edits in the unit itself;
# this file exists for the two that systemd *can* substitute.

# Absolute path to this checkout -- the directory containing this scripts/
# folder. Used to locate scripts/run-camera-server.sh in ExecStart=.
CAMERA_SERVER_CHECKOUT=/home/YOUR_USER/ISEKAI-link

# See docs/Build.md's OpenCV build step for where this points on your
# machine. run-camera-server.sh refuses to start without it rather than
# guessing.
OPENCV_LIB_DIR=/home/YOUR_USER/opencv-4.12-local/lib
